            <ArticleTitle>Acyclic Quaternary Carbon Stereocenters via Enantioselective Transition Metal Catalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12564-12580</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.chemrev.7b00385</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Whereas numerous asymmetric methods for formation of quaternary carbon stereocenters in cyclic systems have been documented, the construction of acyclic quaternary carbon stereocenters with control of absolute stereochemistry remains a formidable challenge. This Review summarizes enantioselective methods for the construction of acyclic quaternary carbon stereocenters from achiral or chiral racemic reactants via transition metal catalysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
